<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Christian IV of Denmark</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1577–1648</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Christian IV was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> from 1588 to 1648. He founded towns such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gluckstadt">Glückstadt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oslo">Christiania</a> and built palaces including Rosenborg in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copenhagen">Copenhagen</a>. His intervention in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War ended in defeat in 1626, and wars with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> cost Denmark Gotland, Ösel and other lands in 1645.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/christian-iv-of-denmark.jpg" alt="Christian IV of Denmark" width="320" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pieter Isaacsz · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Christian_IV_Pieter_Isaacsz_1612.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
